{
  "_readme": [
    "Each country's real international hubs, best first. Consumed by",
    "airports.shortlist() as the primary ranking signal for discovery seeding.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: OurAirports' `type` is a runway/facility category, not a",
    "traffic one, so every serious airport in a country lands in the same 'large'",
    "tier. With scheduled+tier tied, the old sort fell through to the IATA code and",
    "picked each country's ALPHABETICALLY FIRST airport: Turkey probed ADB (Izmir)",
    "instead of IST, the UAE probed AAN (Al Ain) instead of DXB, Japan probed AOJ",
    "(Aomori) instead of HND, Egypt probed AAC (El Arish) instead of CAI. A whole",
    "region's seeding budget went to regional airstrips while the actual hubs were",
    "never probed at all.",
    "",
    "Only the ORDER matters, and in practice only the first entry or two: seeding is",
    "round-robin by country, so entry 0 is what gets probed before any country's",
    "second airport. A country absent from this file falls back to the old",
    "(scheduled, tier, code) ordering, so partial coverage is fine and safe.",
    "",
    "Codes are validated against data/airports.v3.json by",
    "tests/test_airports_data.py - a typo or a code in the wrong country fails there,",
    "and is ignored at runtime rather than probed.",
    "",
    "Keys starting with an underscore are ignored by the loader."
  ],

